  "solution": {
    "text": "A general point on the given line <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> can we taken as <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />If it also lies on the given plane then<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Point of intersection is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> , which lies on <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"
